{title: 383 - O Day of Rest and Gladness}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #383 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 383}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]O day of [Bb7]rest and [Eb]gladness, O  day of joy[Bb7] and lig[Eb]ht,
[Eb]O balm of [Bb7]care and [Eb]sadness, most beautiful,  [Bb7]most bright[Eb];
[Eb]On [Ab]thee, the high and [Eb]lowly, who [Bb7]bend before the t[Eb]hrone,
[Eb]Sing, "[Ab]Holy, holy, [Eb]holy," to the E[Bb7]ter - nal [Eb]One.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Thou [Bb7]art [Eb]a [Bb7]port [Eb]protected
[Eb]From [Bb7]storms [Eb]that [Bb7]round [Eb]us rise;
[Eb][Ab]A [Eb][Bb7]garden [Eb]intersected
[Eb][Ab]With [Eb]streams [Bb7]of [Eb]paradise;
[Eb]Thou [Bb7]art [Eb]a [Bb7]cooling [Eb]fountain
[Eb]In [Bb7]life's [Eb]dry [Bb7]dreary [Eb]sand;
[Eb]From [Ab]Thee, [Eb]like [Bb7]Pisgah's [Eb]mountain,
[Eb]We [Ab]view [Eb]our [Bb7]promised [Eb]land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]A [Bb7]day [Eb]of [Bb7]sweet [Eb]reflection
[Eb]Thou [Bb7]art, [Eb]a [Bb7]day [Eb]of love,
[Eb]A [Ab]day [Eb]to [Bb7]raise [Eb]affection
[Eb]From [Ab]earth [Eb]to [Bb7]things [Eb]above.
[Eb][Bb7]New [Eb]graces [Bb7]ever [Eb]gaining
[Eb]From [Bb7]this [Eb]our [Bb7]day [Eb]of rest,
[Eb]We [Ab]seek [Eb]the [Bb7]rest [Eb]remaining
[Eb]To [Ab]mansions [Eb]of [Bb7]the [Eb]blest.
{end_of_verse}
